31. Contents, date and signature of judgment. The judgment of the Appellate Court shall be 
in writing and shall state__ 
(a) the points for determination; 
(b) the decision thereon; 
(c) the reasons for the decision; and, 
(d) where the decree appealed from is reversed or varied, the relief to which the 
appellant is entitled; 
and shall at the time that it is pronounced be signed and dated by the Judge or by the Judges concurring 
therein.

